<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich Schliemann</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1822–1890</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich Schliemann was a German businessman and pioneering archaeologist who set out to prove the historical basis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a>'s epics. From 1871 he excavated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Hisarlik</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, identifying it as Troy, and in 1876 he found the shaft graves of Mycenae with their gold masks. His methods were destructive, but his discoveries opened the study of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> prehistory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heinrich-schliemann.jpg" alt="Heinrich Schliemann" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ed. Schultze Hofphotograph Heidelberg Plöckstrasse 79 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrich_Schliemann_(HeidICON_28763)_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
